<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.298 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.298 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE DEC 30, 2002</p>
<p>			     $11.500 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.298    Awarded At	99.797	6.250</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.290    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.250    87 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  3.19 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 30.Jun.02</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 30.Jun.97</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 25.Jun.97</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  11.500 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272Y7</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   36.661			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   549.15 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.250</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.060			   PRICE	 99.797</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.250-6.298 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.298</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.616 PCT AT AUCTION ON 29.MAY.97 KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.165 PCT AT AUCTION 19.DEC.96</p>
